'''Humanity Catified''' (人類ネコ化計画, ''Jinrui Neko-ka Kēkaku'', '''Human Catification Project''') is the 48th sub-chapter of [[Uncanny Legends]], and the 97th sub-chapter overall. It was added in [[Version 12.0 Update|Version 12.0]] and is available up to {{4c}} difficulty.

Stages 1-5 are similar to [[Spacetime Distortion]], beginning with rematches against the first four Uncanny Legends drop units followed by a [[Atonement for Sin|single stage]] containing all of them. However, the rematches have completely new support for the bosses, as opposed to recycling old lineups. Clearing stage 5 gives access to the [[True Form]] evolutions of the first four Uncanny Legends drop units and unlocks [[Seven Lights of Doom (Merciless)|Mining Epic]], a stage that drops the necessary Epic [[Catfruit|Behemoth Stones]]. Stages 6-8 drop a combined total of 6 [[Platinum Capsules (Gacha Event)|Platinum Shards]] when cleared for the first time.

==Difficulty==
Stages vary from moderately to extremely difficult, depending on the enemy composition, all made harder by every stage having the [[No Continues]] restriction. The hardest of all is [[Birth of True Man]], where the synergy of [[Great Ape Luza]] and [[Pterowl Hazuku]] can prove extremely difficult to overcome without [[True Form]]s like [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] and [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], unless one stalls at the beginning and waits for the [[Owlbrow]]s and [[Relic Doge]]s to be expended before the boss fight.
{{LegendDiff|110|120|100}}

==New Features==
This subchapter introduces 5 enemies to Uncanny Legends, though only the first is entirely new:
*[[Great Ape Luza]]: A powerful [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemy with a large health pool, monstrous attack power and a dual Omni Strike attack, the second hit capable of reaching units up to 700 range away. Additionally immune to [[Wave Attack|Waves]].
*[[Casaurian Darkjo]]: First time arriving in Uncanny Legends. A [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/Behemoth enemy with a lot of HP and knockbacks with an expanding 3-hit Long-Distance attack up to 351 range. Strong based on stats alone, but made occasionally lethal with his 5% chance to deal Toxic damage to cats for 50% of their health. Also immune to [[Surge Attack|Surges]], Freeze, and Weaken.
*[[Formicidaean Ariant]]: First time arriving in Uncanny Legends. A [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]/Behemoth enemy that is not to be underestimated. Despite its 24-second long revival time, you won't want this insect alive. Its lengthy attack animation ends with overwhelming damage, easily obliterating even the tankiest of cats. Its immunity to Knockback, Freeze, and Weaken ensure that the only way to interrupt it is by brute force.
*[[Cumulus Gallus|Cumulus Gallus:]] First time arriving in Uncanny Legends. A mid-ranged [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]]/Behemoth enemy, incredibly tanky with a strengthen at 33% health! Additionally immune to both Weaken and Slow.
*[[Pterowl Hazuku|Pterowl Hazuku:]] First time arriving in Uncanny Legends. A [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]/Behemoth enemy, it deals heavy damage with an incredible effective range of of 330-1060, nuking hordes of units in one hit. Adding onto this madness, it has a 20% chance to spawn a Lv.1 Surge Attack between 400 and 1200 range and is immune to Surges.

