==Trivia==
*Humanity Catified's Japanese name, Human Catification Project, is likely a reference to the [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Human_Instrumentality_Project Human Instrumentality Project] from ''[[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]''.
*Each of the [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapters]] is represented in stages 6-8 of Humanity Catified:
**The [[Media:Rc164.png|tree]] that serves as the enemy base in all three stages may reference the [[Media:Ec047 ja.png|tree]] from [[wikipedia:Iriomote Island|Iriomote Island]], the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|48th stage]] of the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese Version]] of [[Empire of Cats]], as the phrase 野生の底力 ''yasei no sokojikara'' ("underlying power of the wild") on Iriomote Island's base is also present in the Japanese description of [[Wild Doge]], who appears in the last two stages of Humanity Catified. This is further supported by how Humanity Catified is the 48th sub-chapter of [[Uncanny Legends]].
**[[Reign of the Ape Lord]]'s boss theme is "Apollo Kessen", which was first used in the [[Moon (Into the Future)|Moon]] stage of [[Into the Future]].
**The [[music]] played in [[Ape Lord's Revenge]] is "Big Bang Kumikyoku", which was first used in [[The Big Bang (Cats of the Cosmos)|The Big Bang]] stage of [[Cats of the Cosmos]].
**[[Birth of True Man]]'s boss theme is the [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)|Mount Aku/Mount Fuji Invasion]] theme from [[The Aku Realms]].
*The [[Media:Bg1027.gif|huge, glowing tree]] in the background of stages 6-8 may be a reference to various fictional "[[wikipedia:Tree of life|trees of life]]", such as:
**[[wikipedia:Yggdrasil|Yggdrasil]] from Norse mythology, as [[Urs & Fenrir (Enemy)|Fenrir]] is directly named after [[wikipedia:Fenrir|Fenrir]] from Norse mythology, and Urs and [[Ultima Beast Naala]] may both be based on figures with connections to Yggdrasil: Urs (ウルス ''Urusu'') may be named after [[wikipedia:Urðr|Urðr]] (ウルズ ''Uruzu''), who lives beneath and tends to Yggdrasil, while Naala may be based on [[wikipedia:Eikþyrnir|Eikþyrnir]], who eats from [[wikipedia:Læraðr|Læraðr]]—a tree often identified with Yggdrasil. The dew that drips from Eikþyrnir's glowing antlers flows into [[wikipedia:Hvergelmir|Hvergelmir]], one of the wellsprings at Yggdrasil's roots, creating rivers that sustain life. The tree also appears in [[Revival of Origin]], whose [[Squire Rel]] or [[Sir Rel]] may represent [[wikipedia:Ratatoskr|Ratatoskr]], a messenger squirrel who runs up and down Yggdrasil.
**The [[wikia:Mana:Tree of Mana|Tree of Mana]] from the ''[[wikipedia:Mana (series)|Mana]]'' series, as [[Zero Luza]]'s description mentions energy that makes up all things, much like [[wikia:Mana:Mana (element)|Mana]] itself, and an ancient god appears from the tree in the Uncanny Legends ending, possibly an equivalent to the [[wikia:Mana:Mana Goddess|Mana Goddess]]. This god is implied to be [[Sage of Life Dr. Nova]], who may represent ''[[wikipedia:Legend of Mana|Legend of Mana]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s final boss, the corrupted Mana Goddess.
**The [[wikia:dragonball:Tree of Might|Tree of Might]] from ''[[wikia:dragonball:Dragon Ball Z: The Tree of Might|Dragon Ball Z: The Tree of Might]]'', as both [[Sacred Forest]] and the Tree of Might have the kanji 神 ("divine") in their Japanese names, and one of the only groups that can eat its fruit are the universal deities called the [[wikia:dragonball:Kai|Kais]], again possibly tying into the ancient god mentioned in the Uncanny Legends ending.
**The [[wikia:dragonball:Universe Tree|Universe Tree]] introduced in [[wikia:dragonball:Dragon Ball Heroes|''Dragon Ball Heroes'']], as Uncanny Legends is followed by [[A Whole New World]], which features an [[Metafilibuster (Enemy)|enemy]] based on one of the [[wikia:dragonball:Universe Creation Planners|Universe Creation Planners]].
*Humanity Catified is mentioned in [[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|True Superfeline]]'s and [[Mass Production EVA (Uber Rare Cat)|Mass Production EVA-Cat]]'s descriptions.
*This sub-chapter has the highest number of [[No Continues]] stages, at 8, eclipsing that of all others in non-event Legend Stages.
**It is also the only Uncanny Legends sub-chapter to have more than 6 stages.

